      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the type of curve on which the points \\((x, y) = \\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\) lie, we start by expressing \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in terms of \\(t\\):\n\n\\[x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} = 1 + \\frac{1}{t}\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{t}\\]\n\nNext, we need to eliminate the parameter \\(t\\) to find a relationship between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\). From the expressions for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), we have:\n\n\\[x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\implies \\frac{1}{t} = x - 1 \\implies t = \\frac{1}{x - 1}\\]\n\nSimilarly, substituting \\(t = \\frac{1}{x - 1}\\) into the expression for \\(y\\), we get:\n\n\\[y = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} = 1 - (x - 1) = 2 - x\\]\n\nThus, we have the relationship:\n\n\\[y = 2 - x\\]\n\nThis is the equation of a straight line in the \\(xy\\)-plane. Therefore, all the plotted points lie on a line.\n\nThe correct option is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
